cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Rare Disease Venture & Translational Opportunity Atlas, MyelofibrosisBench-v1, or its molecular/clinical datasets in academic research, deep-research synthesis, or autonomous agent workflows, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Rare Disease Venture & Translational Opportunity Atlas: Clonal JAK2 V617F+ Primary Myelofibrosis & Reversible Autoimmune Myelofibrosis"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Rare Disease Venture Atlas"
    website: "https://rare-disease-atlas.github.io"
version: "1.6.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
url: "https://rare-disease-atlas.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rare-disease-atlas/rare-disease-atlas.github.io"
repository-artifact: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/rare-disease-atlas/rare-disease-venture-atlas"
abstract: >-
  Open-science translational briefing node, Model Context Protocol (MCP) server,
  A2A specialist agent, MyelofibrosisBench-v1 evaluation suite, and structured
  Hugging Face Parquet corpus anchored on Paired Myelofibrosis Flagships:
  (1) Clonal JAK2 V617F+ Primary Myelofibrosis (ORPHA:824, ICD-10-CM D47.4 — JH2
  pseudokinase vs JH1 catalytic selectivity, INCB160058 NCT06313593, AJ1-11095
  NCT06343805, mutant CALR, single-cell marrow cohorts GSE144568 and GSE122198),
  and (2) Reversible JAK2-Negative Autoimmune Myelofibrosis (AIMF, ICD-10-CM
  D75.89 — Nature's Positive Control demonstrating 74-80% human bone marrow
  reticulin fibrosis resolution alongside dual transfusional and IL-6/hepcidin/ferroportin
  iron trapping). Software and MCP/Agent protocols are licensed under MIT;
  datasets and benchmarks are licensed under CC-BY-4.0.
keywords:
  - myelofibrosis
  - JAK2 V617F
  - JH2 pseudokinase
  - autoimmune myelofibrosis
  - AIMF
  - hepcidin
  - iron overload
  - orphan drug
  - rare disease
  - MyelofibrosisBench-v1
  - model-context-protocol
  - computational biology
